// Experiment C1 uprobe stage: the nine prescribed Candidate-1 functions.
//
// // no resolvable probe is replaced at trial time with the probe list that bpftrace can
// actually resolve on this guest's Chromium executable. bpftrace has no
// optional-attach syntax, so a symbol that cannot be resolved is not emitted and
// is instead recorded in the per-trial trace reduction under
// `uprobe_status.unresolved` together with the resolution attempt.
//
// Prescribed set (all nine attempted every trial, identically in both
// conditions):
//   DatabaseConnection::Release
//   DatabaseConnection::MaybeSelfDestruct
//   BackingStoreImpl::DestroyConnection
//   DatabaseConnection::GetCleanupTask
//   DatabaseConnection::CloseDatabase
//   sql::Database::CloseInternal
//   sqlite3WalClose
//   sqlite3WalCheckpoint
//   unixSync
//
// Firing line format (space separated): U NSECS PID TID SYMBOL COMM
//   PID is the thread-group id, TID the thread id, matching the strace `[pid N]`
//   thread id and the eBPF stream's tid so a firing can be joined to a WAL
//   descriptor sync on the shared guest clock.
// no resolvable probe
{
  printf("U %llu %d %d %s %s\n", nsecs, pid, tid, probe, comm);
}
